LANGUAGE English

BOOK ClosePortal ORDERED NO KEEP LOOPED
    IF goal != goalClosePortal THEN EXIT

    // this hides the page since we are NO KEEP
    // this is easier than managing visibility
    MARK Step2Repeat READ

    PAGE Step1
        BUTTON "Begin Ritual"

        PROLOG "
            The portal is open and you must close it quickly. If you have the
            {c:QItemRitualKnife}, the {c:QItemRitualComponents}, and the
            {c:QItemElderSignPendant}, you can start now.
        
            Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can perform this ritual and only
            while standing at the altar.
        
            Are you ready?
        "

        TEXT "
            You flip to the correct place in the book, turn to face the altar, and
            lay out the materials. The pattern is complex and it takes a few
            minutes to get right. Your companions are under constant attack by cult
            members and you can feel the approach of something from the other side
            of the portal. You have to hurry.
    
            Drop the {c:QItemRitualComponents} Unique Item on the altar. It must stay on the altar for the duration of the ritual.
    
            This step is complete.
        "

        ADD QItemRitualComponents
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step2
        BUTTON "Bless the knife"

        PROLOG "
            You turn the page and review the process for <<blessing>> the knife.
            When you glance down, you are suprised that you can read the
            blessing now.

            You pull out the {c:QItemRitualDagger} and...
        "
        TEXT "
            The book shows you how to hold the knife and some kind movement like
            you're presenting it to the altar. You fumble around, hoping your first
            try at something like this will be good enough.

            While you can read the words of the blessing, you aren't sure you
            understand it. If you do, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope
            for the best.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        TEST QUOTA 3
            ON PASS GOTO Step2Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step2Fail
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step2Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            As you finish the incantation, the blade becomes heavier and brighter. It...
            changes. The {c:QItemRitualKnife} is ready for what comes next.
        
            This step is complete
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step2Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You finish the blessing but nothing seems to have happened. You'll need
            to keep trying.
        
            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step2Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step2Repeat
        PROLOG "
            The knife still feels cold and dead in your hand. You're starting to
            wonder if you>>ll really be able to do this. You look at your fellow
            investigators, struggling to keep you alive and look down to try
            again.
        "

        BUTTON "Try again"

        TEXT "
            You scan the text one more time, hold the knife over the altar,
            close your eyes, and speak the words.

            If are certain you understand it now, test {lore}; otherwise, feel While you can read the words of the blessing, you aren't sure you
            understand it. If you do, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope
            for the best.
        "

        TEST QUOTA 4
            ON PASS GOTO Step2Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step2FailRepeat
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step2FailRepeat
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You finish again and... nothing. You take a breath to calm your
            nerves, but noise and horror across the room make it hard to focus.
        
            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step2Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step3
        PROLOG "
            You turn the page and see the next step: drawing blood. You have to cut
            yourself with the {c:QItemRitualDagger} and let the blood drip into the
            chalice on the altar. The book says that the blood will empower the
            ritual and help close the portal.
    
            You look at your hand and realize you are going to have to do this more
            than once. You steel yourself and prepare to draw blood.
        "

        TEXT "
            You grip the {c:QItemRitualDagger} tightly and prepare to draw blood. You
            can feel your heart pounding in your chest. You have to do this. You have
            to stop the ritual.

            Test {will}. For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        TEST QUOTA 3
            ON PASS GOTO Step3Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step3Fail
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step3Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You squeeze your hand into a tight fist and blood drips into the chalice.
            You can>t see or hear the chalice change, but you can feel something
            happen to it.

            This step is complete.
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step3Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            A drop of blood spatters when it hits the cup, but nothing seems to
            happen. You're going to have to slice deeper.
        
            Suffer 2 Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step3 UNREAD
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step4
        PROLOG "
            The portal is humming and pulsing with energy. You can feel something
            trying to get through from the other side. You have to hurry.
            You turn the page and see the next incantation. Like the blessing, you
            can read it, but you aren>t sure you understand it.
        "

        BUTTON "Read the incantation"

        TEXT "
            The first incantation is long and complex. You>ll have to get this
            right to weaken the portal. If you don>t, it will take longer to
            close and the onslaught from the other side isn't abating. You close
            your eyes for a moment, take a deep breath, then look at the text
            and begin to read the incantation aloud.

            If you understand it, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope for
            the best.
       "
   
       TEST QUOTA 5
            ON PASS GOTO Step4Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step4Fail
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step4Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You feel a welling of power as you speak the last word. The feeling
            inside you grows and you suddenly feel like you control the cosmos.
            The portal grows brighter and {c:TokenPortal} screams. You had
            forgotten about the boy--he will die in this ritual.
        
            Suffer 1 facedown Horror.
        
            As the scream echos in the room, the portal grows dimmer and shrinks
            slightly. Where it was humming and stable before, it is sputtering,
            pulsing erratically, and making an electrical sound. It has been
            weakened, but not closed. It will eventually collapse on its own,
            but you can still feel something approaching. You can do better.
        
            This step is complete.
        "
    
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step4Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You can feel something happen inside but it is not very strong and the
            portal has not changed. You'll have to try the incantation again.
            The ritual is wearing you down.
        
            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step4Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step4Repeat
        PROLOG "
            The portal is still humming and pulsing with energy. Whatever is
            approaching is getting closer.
        
            You look at the incantation again. Like the blessing, you can read it,
            but you aren>t sure you understand it.
        "

        BUTTON "Try again"

        TEXT "
            Your fellow investigators are struggling to keep you alive and one
            looks over at you with panic in their eyes. You have to get this. You
            look down at the text again.
        
             If you understand it, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope for
             the best.
        "
        TEST QUOTA 2
            ON PASS GOTO Step4Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step4Fail
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step5
        PROLOG "
            You turn the page and see the next step: you'll need more blood. You
            have to cut yourself again with the {c:QItemRitualDagger} and let the
            blood drip on to the {c:QItemElderSign}. The book says that the blood
            will empower the {c:QItemElderSign} to completely close the portal.
    
            You look at your hand and see that it has stopped bleeding. Cutting
            yourself again will take courage.
        "

        BUTTON "Draw more blood"

        TEXT "
            You draw your knife across your palm again and a searing pain
            momentarily overwhelms you. You have to do this.

            You look back down at the book and speak.

            If you understand the text, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and
            hope for the best.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        TEST QUOTA 4
            ON PASS GOTO Step5Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step5Fail
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step5Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You squeeze your hand into a tight fist over the trinket. As your blood
            drips, the it begins to glow. Then it and the knife slowly pulse. When
            you look up, you see the portal is dimmer and smaller, pulsing with the
            knife, {c:QItemElderSign}, and now the skull. The boy begins screaming
            again, no longer sounding human.

            The {c:QItemElderSign} rises and hovers over the altar. It vibrates
            briefly, then slowly moves across the room toward the portal.

            The boy screams one last time as the elder sign makes contact with his
            forehead. The boy goes rigid, then the portal collapses and the boy
            falls to the ground... still smoldering... still moaning.
        
            The investigation is over.
        "

        result = fullWin
        GOTO EventGameOverStart
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step5Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You finish the incantation, but nothing seems to happen. You>ll have
            to try again.

            Suffer 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step5Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE

    PAGE Step5Repeat
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        PROLOG "
            You lift your hand over the altar again and prepare to speak again.
            The boy is still screaming in pain and terror.
        "

        BUTTON "Try again"

        TEXT "
            You sqeeze more blood out of your fist on to the {c:QItemElderSign}.
            As it hit the trinket, the boy stops screaming.

            Test {lore} or {will}.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        TEST QUOTA 4
            ON PASS GOTO Step5Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step5Fail
    END PAGE

END BOOK